      "id": "44",
      "title": "Why Intangible Cultural Heritage Fascinates Me: A Story About Human Behavior, Not Just Tradition",
      "excerpt": "Most people think Intangible Cultural Heritage is about dances, music, rituals, and craftsmanship. It is — but those are only the visible outcomes. What fascinates me is the invisible system underneath: human behavior. This is a personal reflection on how a lesson from my father, delivered without a single explanation, taught me to read culture as an accumulation of human decisions — and how nine behavioral science theories, from Bandura to Ostrom, quietly explain why some traditions survive for centuries while others vanish within a single generation.",
      "category": "Reflection - Heritage & Behavioral Science",
      "date": "July 29, 2026",
      "imageUrl": "thum/ICHBehavioralScience.png",
      "slug": "why-intangible-cultural-heritage-fascinates-me-a-story-about-human-behavior-not-just-tradition"
