      "excerpt": "UNESCO catalogs the dances, the crafts, the festivals — but rarely the quiet social technologies that keep a community from tearing itself apart after a conflict. A tour through Japan's Wa, China's He, Korea's Jeong, and Java's Tepa Selira, a look at Japan's own two-edged system for when harmony breaks down, and why \"living heritage\" was never supposed to require a UNESCO inscription to be real.",
